[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m# fux-vt-compare: fux-vt beside other terminal emulators                                                                [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m                                                                                                                        [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mAn excluded package with its own lockfile. It runs fux-vt beside a panel of                                             [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mother terminal emulators ("engines"):                                                                                   [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m                                                                                                                        [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m- engines linked into the binary: Ghostty's core (libghostty-vt), alacritty_terminal,                                   [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m  libvterm, avt, wezterm-term and the vt100 crate;                                                                      [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m- engines run as processes of their own: xterm.js (`@xterm/headless` under                                              [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m  Node), tmux, and xterm itself under Xvfb.                                                                             [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m                                                                                                                        [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mEvery engine gets the same output. After each piece of it, and each resize,                                             [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0meach engine's screen is compared with fux-vt's, cell by cell, along with the                                            [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mcursor, the modes, soft wraps, the title, cursor reports and recent history.                                            [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mfux-vt fails a case only where the engines outvote it (see "The vote"). A                                               [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mfailing case is shrunk to the smallest one that still fails and printed with                                            [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mthe command that replays it. `bench` times every engine on the same                                                     [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mworkloads. The corpus (`corpus/`) holds what real programs wrote to a                                                   [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mterminal, recorded by `record`.                                                                                         [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m                                                                                                                        [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mIt is not built or run by fux's own gates. It needs Zig, a Ghostty                                                      [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mcheckout, libvterm's source and, for the engines in their own processes,                                                [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mNode, tmux, xterm and Xvfb. `run.sh` fetches the first three.                                                           [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m                                                                                                                        [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mNo engine is the truth. When the panel outvotes fux-vt, the difference says                                             [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mwhere to look. xterm's behaviour and the standards decide which side is                                                 [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mright. Some differences are choices fux-vt makes on purpose, and each family                                            [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mbelow records which.                                                                                                    [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m                                                                                                                        [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m## Running it                                                                                                           [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m                                                                                                                        [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0m```sh                                                                                                                   [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mfux-vt/compare/run.sh                       # families expected to agree, 20000 cases, beside the panel                 [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mfux-vt/compare/run.sh engines               # which engines run here, which vote, what each cannot tell                 [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mfux-vt/compare/run.sh cases                 # the named cases beside every engine, with each engine's mark              [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mfux-vt/compare/run.sh verdicts              # the families with a recorded verdict, beside the engines that decide each [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mfux-vt/compare/run.sh matrix                # family by engine: % of cases each engine differs from fux-vt              [39;49m
[A
[38;2;255;255;255m[48;2;0;0;0mfux-vt/compare/run.sh bench                 # MB/s for every engine on every workload, and the corpus                   [39;49m
